> I have a lot more food in the bag.  I have a stash of about 50,000zm on
> lvl18 (thanks to a little trip to the Ft).

Once you've cleared the level below the castle, haul the gold down
there: there's a temple which will accept donations.

> Lots more wands (espeically
> magic misslle, striking, and teleport).

Attack spells from wands are largely useless in the later stages of
the game. Use your own spells and delegate wands to utility usage
(breaking boulders, engraving, un-sliming).

[the eye]
> Now it just
> ignores me.

Wait a while. Then wait some more. Invokable items have a timeout, and
if you try to invoke them before that time is up, they will 'ignore
you' and slap a couple more turns onto the running timeout. Don't keep
trying, that will only make matters worse.

> Also Nefert won't get off the throne. 

Move towards her and abort the attempt to attack (not a good idea when
confused or wielding Stormbringer, because then you _won't_ abort).
Alternatively, a _tough_ pet and conflict or an instadeath method can
forcibly remove her. In the latter case, you'll suffer a big alignment
hit, but that's easy to correct.

> Now the horrors of Gehennom.  First, am I ready?  From the spoilers
> I've read, I don't think so.  Hp and Pw seem awfully low. 

For a wizard, they're absolutely sufficient. AC looks like more of a
problem for a first foray into Gehennom, but a donation session should
put you close to -20, which should be enough for everything before the
endgame.

> I also have
> a nagging feeling that I'm missing something.

You will, in the fullness of time, need a way to detect traps and to
levitate; having a few (that's 2-4, _not_ 20-30) potions of full
healing is recommended, as well as a charged wand of fire. Conflict is
useful and amusing. Pets can be a great help.

